title: Error Codes
id: errors
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"html","value":"<!-- Generated by scripts/generate-error-docs.mjs. Do not edit by hand. -->"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production builds of TanStack DB shorten error messages to a code, the inputs\nthat the error can show, and a link to this page. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"TanStack DB error 17 (key=1, collectionId=\"todos\"): https://tanstack.com/db/latest/docs/errors#error-17","lang":"text"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A console warning uses the same form with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"warning"},{"type":"text","value":" in place of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":".\nDevelopment builds keep the full messages below. The error classes, their\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" values, and their fields are the same in both builds. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./guides/error-handling.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for how to catch them."}]},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-2\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-2-duplicatedbinstanceerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 2: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DuplicateDbInstanceError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Multiple instances of @tanstack/db detected!\n\nThis causes transaction context to be lost because each instance maintains its own transaction stack.\n\nCommon causes:\n1. Different versions of @tanstack/db installed\n2. Incompatible peer dependency versions in packages\n3. Module resolution issues in bundler configuration\n\nTo fix:\n1. Check installed versions: npm list @tanstack/db (or pnpm/yarn list)\n2. Force a single version using package manager overrides:\n   - npm: \"overrides\" in package.json\n   - pnpm: \"pnpm.overrides\" in package.json\n   - yarn: \"resolutions\" in package.json\n3. Clear node_modules and lockfile, then reinstall\n\nTo temporarily disable this check (not recommended):\nSet environment variable: TANSTACK_DB_DISABLE_DUP_CHECK=1\n\nSee: https://tanstack.com/db/latest/docs/troubleshooting#duplicate-instances","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-3\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-3-invalidsyncpersistencecapabilityerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 3: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InvalidSyncPersistenceCapabilityError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Invalid sync persistence capability at metadata.persistence: reason. Custom sync wrappers must forward metadata.persistence unchanged.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-4\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-4-collectionrequiresconfigerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 4: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionRequiresConfigError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Collection requires a config","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-5\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-5-collectionrequiressyncconfigerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 5: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionRequiresSyncConfigError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Collection requires a sync config","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-6\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-6-invalidschemaerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 6: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InvalidSchemaError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Schema must implement the standard-schema interface","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-7\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-7-schemamustbesynchronouserror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 7: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SchemaMustBeSynchronousError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Schema validation must be synchronous","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-8\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-8-collectioninerrorstateerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 8: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionInErrorStateError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Cannot perform operation on collection \"collection-1\" - collection is in error state. Try calling cleanup() and restarting the collection.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-9\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-9-invalidcollectionstatustransitionerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 9: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InvalidCollectionStatusTransitionError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Invalid collection status transition from \"pending\" to \"ready\" for collection \"collection-1\"","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-10\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-10-collectionisinerrorstateerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 10: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionIsInErrorStateError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Collection is in error state","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-11\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-11-negativeactivesubscriberserror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 11: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NegativeActiveSubscribersError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Active subscribers count is negative - this should never happen","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-12\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-12-livequeryobserverdisposederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 12: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LiveQueryObserverDisposedError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Cannot subscribe to a disposed LiveQueryObserver","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-13\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-13-livequerywindowcontrollerdisposederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 13: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LiveQueryWindowControllerDisposedError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Cannot subscribe to a disposed LiveQueryWindowController","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-14\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-14-undefinedkeyerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 14: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UndefinedKeyError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"An object was created without a defined key: {\"name\":\"item\"}","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-15\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-15-invalidkeyerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 15: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InvalidKeyError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getKey returned an invalid key type. Expected string or number, but got null: null. Item: {\"name\":\"item\"}","lang":"text"},{"type":"code","value":"getKey returned an invalid key type. Expected string or number, but got object: {\"id\":1}. Item: {\"name\":\"item\"}","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-16\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-16-duplicatekeyerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 16: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DuplicateKeyError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Cannot insert document with ID \"key-1\" because it already exists in the collection","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-17\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-17-duplicatekeysyncerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 17: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DuplicateKeySyncError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Cannot insert document with key \"123\" from sync because it already exists in the collection \"collection-1\"","lang":"text"},{"type":"code","value":"Cannot insert document with key \"key-1\" from sync because it already exists in the collection \"collection-1\". This collection uses a custom getKey with .distinct(). The .distinct() operator deduplicates by the ENTIRE selected object (standard SQL behavior), but your custom getKey extracts only a subset of fields. This causes multiple distinct rows (with different values in non-key fields) to receive the same key. To fix this, either: (1) ensure your SELECT only includes fields that uniquely identify each row, (2) use .groupBy() with min()/max() aggregates to select one value per group, or (3) remove the custom getKey to use the default key behavior.","lang":"text"},{"type":"code","value":"Cannot insert document with key \"key-1\" from sync because it already exists in the collection \"collection-1\". This collection uses a custom getKey with joined queries. Joined queries can produce multiple rows with the same key when relationships are not 1:1. Consider: (1) using a composite key in your getKey function (e.g., `${item.key1}-${item.key2}`), (2) ensuring your join produces unique rows per key, or (3) removing the custom getKey to use the default composite key behavior.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-18\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-18-missingupdateargumenterror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 18: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MissingUpdateArgumentError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"The first argument to update is missing","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-19\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-19-nokeyspassedtoupdateerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 19: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoKeysPassedToUpdateError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"No keys were passed to update","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-20\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-20-updatekeynotfounderror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 20: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UpdateKeyNotFoundError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"The key \"key-1\" was passed to update but an object for this key was not found in the collection","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-21\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-21-keyupdatenotallowederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 21: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyUpdateNotAllowedError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Updating the key of an item is not allowed. Original key: \"old-key\", Attempted new key: \"new-key\". Please delete the old item and create a new one if a key change is necessary.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-22\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-22-nokeyspassedtodeleteerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 22: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoKeysPassedToDeleteError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"No keys were passed to delete","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-23\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-23-deletekeynotfounderror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 23: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DeleteKeyNotFoundError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Collection.delete was called with key 'key-1' but there is no item in the collection with this key","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-24\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-24-missinginserthandlererror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 24: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MissingInsertHandlerError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Collection.insert called directly (not within an explicit transaction) but no 'onInsert' handler is configured.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-25\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-25-missingupdatehandlererror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 25: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MissingUpdateHandlerError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Collection.update called directly (not within an explicit transaction) but no 'onUpdate' handler is configured.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-26\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-26-missingdeletehandlererror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 26: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MissingDeleteHandlerError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Collection.delete called directly (not within an explicit transaction) but no 'onDelete' handler is configured.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-27\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-27-queuecapacityexceedederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 27: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueueCapacityExceededError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Queue capacity exceeded; the mutation was not admitted","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-28\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-28-queuedisposederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 28: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueueDisposedError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Queue has been cleaned up; the mutation was not admitted","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-29\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-29-throttlecalldroppederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 29: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThrottleCallDroppedError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Throttle call was dropped because trailing execution is disabled","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-30\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-30-debouncecalldroppederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 30: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DebounceCallDroppedError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Debounce call was dropped because trailing execution is disabled","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-31\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-31-missingmutationfunctionerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 31: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MissingMutationFunctionError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"mutationFn is required when creating a transaction","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-32\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-32-onmutatemustbesynchronouserror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 32: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OnMutateMustBeSynchronousError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onMutate must be synchronous and cannot return a promise. Remove async/await or returned promises from onMutate.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-33\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-33-transactionnotpendingmutateerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 33: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransactionNotPendingMutateError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"You can no longer call .mutate() as the transaction is no longer pending","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-34\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-34-transactionalreadycompletedrollbackerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 34: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransactionAlreadyCompletedRollbackError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"You can no longer call .rollback() as the transaction is already completed","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-35\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-35-transactionnotpendingcommiterror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 35: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransactionNotPendingCommitError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"You can no longer call .commit() as the transaction is no longer pending","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-36\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-36-nopendingsynctransactionwriteerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 36: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoPendingSyncTransactionWriteError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"No pending sync transaction to write to","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-37\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-37-synctransactionalreadycommittedwriteerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 37: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncTransactionAlreadyCommittedWriteError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"The pending sync transaction is already committed, you can't still write to it.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-38\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-38-syncrowreusedwithoutpreviousvalueerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 38: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncRowReusedWithoutPreviousValueError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"A sync update for key \"key-1\" wrote a row object that changed in place since it was last written. The change overwrote the row's previous value. Write a new object, or pass the row's previous value as `previousValue`.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-39\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-39-nopendingsynctransactioncommiterror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 39: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoPendingSyncTransactionCommitError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"No pending sync transaction to commit","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-40\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-40-synctransactionalreadycommittederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 40: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncTransactionAlreadyCommittedError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"The pending sync transaction is already committed, you can't commit it again.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-41\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-41-syncqueueinvarianterror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 41: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncQueueInvariantError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Sync queue invariant failed: invariant detail","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-42\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-42-onlyonesourceallowederror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 42: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OnlyOneSourceAllowedError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Only one source is allowed in the join clause","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-43\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-43-subquerymusthavefromclauseerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 43: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SubQueryMustHaveFromClauseError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"A sub query passed to a join clause must have a from clause itself","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-44\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-44-invalidsourceerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 44: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InvalidSourceError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Invalid source for live query: The value provided for alias \"todos\" is not a Collection or subquery. Live queries only accept Collection instances or subqueries. Please ensure you're passing a valid Collection or QueryBuilder, not a plain array or other data type.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-45\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-45-invalidsourcetypeerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 45: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InvalidSourceTypeError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Invalid source for from clause: Expected an object with a single key-value pair like { alias: collection }. For example: .from({ todos: todosCollection }). Got: string","lang":"text"},{"type":"code","value":"Invalid source for join clause: Expected an object with a single key-value pair like { alias: collection }. For example: .join({ todos: todosCollection }, ({ todo, todos }) => eq(todo.id, todos.id)). Got: number","lang":"text"},{"type":"code","value":"Invalid source for unionAll clause: Expected an object with one or more key-value pairs like { alias: collection }. For example: .unionAll({ todos: todosCollection, events: eventsCollection }). Got: undefined","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-46\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-46-joinconditionmustbeequalityerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 46: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JoinConditionMustBeEqualityError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Join condition must be an equality expression or a nonempty conjunction of equality expressions","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-47\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-47-querymusthavefromclauseerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 47: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryMustHaveFromClauseError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Query must have a from clause","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-48\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-48-invalidwhereexpressionerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 48: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InvalidWhereExpressionError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Invalid where() expression: Expected a query expression, but received a boolean. This usually happens when using JavaScript's comparison operators (===, !==, <, >, etc.) directly. Instead, use the query builder functions:\n\n  ❌ .where(({ user }) => user.id === 'abc')\n  ✅ .where(({ user }) => eq(user.id, 'abc'))\n\nAvailable comparison functions: eq, gt, gte, lt, lte, and, or, not, like, ilike, isNull, isUndefined","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-49\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-49-unsafealiaspatherror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 49: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UnsafeAliasPathError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Unsafe alias path segment \"__proto__\" is not allowed in .select(). Aliases must not contain \"__proto__\", \"prototype\", or \"constructor\".","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-50\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-50-distinctrequiresselecterror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 50: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DistinctRequiresSelectError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"DISTINCT requires a SELECT clause.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-51\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-51-fnselectwithgroupbyerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 51: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FnSelectWithGroupByError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"fn.select() cannot be used with groupBy(). groupBy requires the compiler to statically analyze aggregate functions (count, sum, max, etc.) in the SELECT clause, which is not possible with fn.select() since it is an opaque function. Use .select() instead of .fn.select() when combining with groupBy().","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-52\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-52-unsupportedfnselectresulterror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 52: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UnsupportedFnSelectResultError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"fn.select() cannot return query builder. Child query builders, query expressions, and helpers such as eq(), toArray(), materialize(), concat(toArray()), and caseWhen() are query-construction values. Use them as direct fields in .select() instead.","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-53\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-53-unsupportedrootscalarselecterror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 53: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UnsupportedRootScalarSelectError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Top-level scalar select() is not supported by createLiveQueryCollection() or queryOnce(). Return an object from .select(), or use the scalar query inside toArray(...) or concat(toArray(...)).","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-54\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-54-havingrequiresgroupbyerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 54: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HavingRequiresGroupByError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"HAVING clause requires GROUP BY clause","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"error-55\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-55-limitoffsetrequireorderbyerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error 55: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LimitOffsetRequireOrderByError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development builds show the full message. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"LIMIT and OFFSET require an ORDER BY clause to ensure deterministic results","lang":"text"},{"type":"html","value