`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nNo secure random number generator available: neither crypto.randomUUID nor crypto.getRandomValues is defined in this environment.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-172\"></a>\n\n## Error 172: `query/live/collection-config-builder.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nSource collection '${collectionId}' entered error state\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-173\"></a>\n\n## Error 173: `collection/lifecycle.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n${syncFailure ? Adapter cleanup and local teardown both failed : Multiple local teardown steps failed}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-174\"></a>\n\n## Error 174: `transactions.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nMutation callback and restoration failed\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-179\"></a>\n\n## Error 179: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nIndexedDB is not available in this environment. Ensure you are running in a browser or provide a custom IDBFactory for testing.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-182\"></a>\n\n## Error 182: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to open IndexedDB database \"${name}\": ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-183\"></a>\n\n## Error 183: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nDatabase upgrade failed for \"${name}\": ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-184\"></a>\n\n## Error 184: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to open IndexedDB database \"${name}\": ${errorMessage}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-185\"></a>\n\n## Error 185: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nCannot create object store \"${storeName}\": This operation is only allowed during a database upgrade. Ensure you are calling createObjectStore within the onUpgrade callback of openDatabase.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-186\"></a>\n\n## Error 186: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nObject store \"${storeName}\" already exists in the database. Check the database version and only create stores when needed.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-187\"></a>\n\n## Error 187: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to create object store \"${storeName}\": ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-188\"></a>\n\n## Error 188: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to create transaction for stores [${storeNamesArray.join(', ')}]: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-189\"></a>\n\n## Error 189: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nObject store \"${storeName}\" not found in the database. Ensure the store was created during the database upgrade.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-190\"></a>\n\n## Error 190: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nTransaction was aborted\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-191\"></a>\n\n## Error 191: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to delete IndexedDB database \"${name}\": ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-192\"></a>\n\n## Error 192: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to delete IndexedDB database \"${name}\": ${errorMessage}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-193\"></a>\n\n## Error 193: `indexed-db.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\ncreateIndexedDB requires at least one store in the stores array.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-194\"></a>\n\n## Error 194: `indexed-db.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\ncreateIndexedDB stores array contains duplicate store names.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-195\"></a>\n\n## Error 195: `indexed-db.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nThe \"_versions\" store is reserved for IndexedDB Collection metadata.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-196\"></a>\n\n## Error 196: `indexed-db.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\ncreateIndexedDB stores array contains invalid store names. Each store name must be a non-empty string.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-197\"></a>\n\n## Error 197: `indexed-db.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nIndexedDB connection \"${name}\" closed. Recreate its Collections with a new database instance.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-198\"></a>\n\n## Error 198: `indexed-db.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nThe \"_versions\" store is reserved for IndexedDB Collection metadata.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-199\"></a>\n\n## Error 199: `indexed-db.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nDuplicate imported key: ${key}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-200\"></a>\n\n## Error 200: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to get all keys from object store \"${objectStore.name}\": ${cause}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-201\"></a>\n\n## Error 201: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to write item to object store \"${objectStore.name}\": ${cause}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-202\"></a>\n\n## Error 202: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to delete item with key \"${String(key)}\" from object store \"${objectStore.name}\": ${cause}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-203\"></a>\n\n## Error 203: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to clear object store \"${objectStore.name}\": ${cause}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-204\"></a>\n\n## Error 204: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to get all items from object store \"${objectStore.name}\": ${cause}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-205\"></a>\n\n## Error 205: `indexed-db-wrapper.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to get item with key \"${String(key)}\" from object store \"${objectStore.name}\": ${cause}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-206\"></a>\n\n## Error 206: `collection/index.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nautoIndex: 'eager' requires defaultIndexType to be set. Import an index type and set it:\n  import { BasicIndex } from '@tanstack/db'\n  createCollection({ defaultIndexType: BasicIndex, autoIndex: 'eager', ... })\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-207\"></a>\n\n## Error 207: `collection/indexes.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nNo index type specified and no defaultIndexType set on collection. Either pass indexType in config, or set defaultIndexType on the collection:\n  import { BasicIndex } from '@tanstack/db'\n  createCollection({ defaultIndexType: BasicIndex, ... })\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-208\"></a>\n\n## Error 208: `collection/lifecycle.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nYou can't directly call \"setStatus('ready'). You must use markReady instead.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-209\"></a>\n\n## Error 209: `collection/lifecycle.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nCannot start collection \"${this.id}\" during cleanup. Restart after cleanup() completes.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-210\"></a>\n\n## Error 210: `collection/sync.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nCollection \"${this.id}\" is configured with syncMode \"on-demand\" but the sync function did not return a loadSubset handler. Either provide a loadSubset handler or use syncMode \"eager\".\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-211\"></a>\n\n## Error 211: `query/compiler/index.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nQuery uses alias \"${alias}\" more than once. Give each source in one query a distinct alias.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-212\"></a>\n\n## Error 212: `query/live/collection-config-builder.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nLive query graph failed\n```\n\n<a id=\"warning-213\"></a>\n\n## Warning 213: `collection/change-events.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n${collection.id ? `[${collection.id}] ` : ``}Error processing where clause, falling back to full scan:\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-214\"></a>\n\n## Error 214: `collection/cleanup-queue.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nError in CleanupQueue task:\n```\n\n<a id=\"warning-215\"></a>\n\n## Warning 215: `indexes/auto-index.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n${collection.id ? `[${collection.id}] ` : ``}Failed to create auto-index for field path \"${fieldPath.join(`.`)}\":\n```\n\n<a id=\"warning-216\"></a>\n\n## Warning 216: `indexes/base-index.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to evaluate index expression for key ${key} during removal:\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-218\"></a>\n\n## Error 218: `local-storage.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[LocalStorageCollection] Error saving data to storage key \"${config.storageKey}\":\n```\n\n<a id=\"warning-219\"></a>\n\n## Warning 219: `local-storage.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[LocalStorageCollection] Error loading data from storage key \"${storageKey}\":\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-220\"></a>\n\n## Error 220: `query/effect.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[Effect '${id}'] onSourceError callback threw:\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-221\"></a>\n\n## Error 221: `query/effect.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[Effect '${id}'] ${error.message}. Disposing effect.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-222\"></a>\n\n## Error 222: `query/effect.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[Effect '${id}'] failed to dispose after a source error:\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-223\"></a>\n\n## Error 223: `query/effect.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[Effect '${id}'] failed to dispose after a startup error:\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-224\"></a>\n\n## Error 224: `query/effect.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[Effect] Error in onError handler:\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-225\"></a>\n\n## Error 225: `query/effect.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[Effect] Original error:\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-226\"></a>\n\n## Error 226: `query/effect.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[Effect] Unhandled error in handler:\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-228\"></a>\n\n## Error 228: `query/live/collection-config-builder.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nSubset demand '${planId}' failed: ${normalized.message}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-229\"></a>\n\n## Error 229: `query/live/collection-config-builder.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nInitial subset load failed: ${normalized.message}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-230\"></a>\n\n## Error 230: `local-storage.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nLocalStorage options can create only one Collection. Create fresh options for each Collection.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-231\"></a>\n\n## Error 231: `local-storage.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nLocalStorage manual acceptance belongs to a different Collection.\n```\n\n<a id=\"warning-232\"></a>\n\n## Warning 232: `local-storage.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\n[LocalStorageCollection] Error refreshing a same-tab peer for storage key \"${key}\":\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Error Codes\nid: errors\n---\n\n<!-- Generated by scripts/generate-error-docs.mjs. Do not edit by hand. -->\n\nProduction builds of TanStack DB shorten error messages to a code, the inputs\nthat the error can show, and a link to this page. For example:\n\n```text\nTanStack DB error 17 (key=1, collectionId=\"todos\"): https://tanstack.com/db/latest/docs/errors#error-17\n```\n\nA console warning uses the same form with `warning` in place of `error`.\nDevelopment builds keep the full messages below. The error classes, their\n`name` values, and their fields are the same in both builds. See\n[Error Handling](./guides/error-handling.md) for how to catch them.\n\n<a id=\"error-2\"></a>\n\n## Error 2: `DuplicateDbInstanceError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nMultiple instances of @tanstack/db detected!\n\nThis causes transaction context to be lost because each instance maintains its own transaction stack.\n\nCommon causes:\n1. Different versions of @tanstack/db installed\n2. Incompatible peer dependency versions in packages\n3. Module resolution issues in bundler configuration\n\nTo fix:\n1. Check installed versions: npm list @tanstack/db (or pnpm/yarn list)\n2. Force a single version using package manager overrides:\n   - npm: \"overrides\" in package.json\n   - pnpm: \"pnpm.overrides\" in package.json\n   - yarn: \"resolutions\" in package.json\n3. Clear node_modules and lockfile, then reinstall\n\nTo temporarily disable this check (not recommended):\nSet environment variable: TANSTACK_DB_DISABLE_DUP_CHECK=1\n\nSee: https://tanstack.com/db/latest/docs/troubleshooting#duplicate-instances\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-3\"></a>\n\n## Error 3: `InvalidSyncPersistenceCapabilityError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid sync persistence capability at metadata.persistence: reason. Custom sync wrappers must forward metadata.persistence unchanged.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-4\"></a>\n\n## Error 4: `CollectionRequiresConfigError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection requires a config\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-5\"></a>\n\n## Error 5: `CollectionRequiresSyncConfigError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection requires a sync config\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-6\"></a>\n\n## Error 6: `InvalidSchemaError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nSchema must implement the standard-schema interface\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-7\"></a>\n\n## Error 7: `SchemaMustBeSynchronousError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nSchema validation must be synchronous\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-8\"></a>\n\n## Error 8: `CollectionInErrorStateError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCannot perform operation on collection \"collection-1\" - collection is in error state. Try calling cleanup() and restarting the collection.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-9\"></a>\n\n## Error 9: `InvalidCollectionStatusTransitionError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid collection status transition from \"pending\" to \"ready\" for collection \"collection-1\"\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-10\"></a>\n\n## Error 10: `CollectionIsInErrorStateError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection is in error state\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-11\"></a>\n\n## Error 11: `NegativeActiveSubscribersError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nActive subscribers count is negative - this should never happen\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-12\"></a>\n\n## Error 12: `LiveQueryObserverDisposedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCannot subscribe to a disposed LiveQueryObserver\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-13\"></a>\n\n## Error 13: `LiveQueryWindowControllerDisposedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCannot subscribe to a disposed LiveQueryWindowController\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-14\"></a>\n\n## Error 14: `UndefinedKeyError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nAn object was created without a defined key: {\"name\":\"item\"}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-15\"></a>\n\n## Error 15: `InvalidKeyError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\ngetKey returned an invalid key type. Expected string or number, but got null: null. Item: {\"name\":\"item\"}\n```\n\n```text\ngetKey returned an invalid key type. Expected string or number, but got object: {\"id\":1}. Item: {\"name\":\"item\"}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-16\"></a>\n\n## Error 16: `DuplicateKeyError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCannot insert document with ID \"key-1\" because it already exists in the collection\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-17\"></a>\n\n## Error 17: `DuplicateKeySyncError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCannot insert document with key \"123\" from sync because it already exists in the collection \"collection-1\"\n```\n\n```text\nCannot insert document with key \"key-1\" from sync because it already exists in the collection \"collection-1\". This collection uses a custom getKey with .distinct(). The .distinct() operator deduplicates by the ENTIRE selected object (standard SQL behavior), but your custom getKey extracts only a subset of fields. This causes multiple distinct rows (with different values in non-key fields) to receive the same key. To fix this, either: (1) ensure your SELECT only includes fields that uniquely identify each row, (2) use .groupBy() with min()/max() aggregates to select one value per group, or (3) remove the custom getKey to use the default key behavior.\n```\n\n```text\nCannot insert document with key \"key-1\" from sync because it already exists in the collection \"collection-1\". This collection uses a custom getKey with joined queries. Joined queries can produce multiple rows with the same key when relationships are not 1:1. Consider: (1) using a composite key in your getKey function (e.g., `${item.key1}-${item.key2}`), (2) ensuring your join produces unique rows per key, or (3) removing the custom getKey to use the default composite key behavior.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-18\"></a>\n\n## Error 18: `MissingUpdateArgumentError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nThe first argument to update is missing\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-19\"></a>\n\n## Error 19: `NoKeysPassedToUpdateError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nNo keys were passed to update\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-20\"></a>\n\n## Error 20: `UpdateKeyNotFoundError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nThe key \"key-1\" was passed to update but an object for this key was not found in the collection\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-21\"></a>\n\n## Error 21: `KeyUpdateNotAllowedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUpdating the key of an item is not allowed. Original key: \"old-key\", Attempted new key: \"new-key\". Please delete the old item and create a new one if a key change is necessary.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-22\"></a>\n\n## Error 22: `NoKeysPassedToDeleteError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nNo keys were passed to delete\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-23\"></a>\n\n## Error 23: `DeleteKeyNotFoundError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection.delete was called with key 'key-1' but there is no item in the collection with this key\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-24\"></a>\n\n## Error 24: `MissingInsertHandlerError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection.insert called directly (not within an explicit transaction) but no 'onInsert' handler is configured.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-25\"></a>\n\n## Error 25: `MissingUpdateHandlerError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection.update called directly (not within an explicit transaction) but no 'onUpdate' handler is configured.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-26\"></a>\n\n## Error 26: `MissingDeleteHandlerError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection.delete called directly (not within an explicit transaction) but no 'onDelete' handler is configured.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-27\"></a>\n\n## Error 27: `QueueCapacityExceededError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nQueue capacity exceeded; the mutation was not admitted\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-28\"></a>\n\n## Error 28: `QueueDisposedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nQueue has been cleaned up; the mutation was not admitted\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-29\"></a>\n\n## Error 29: `ThrottleCallDroppedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nThrottle call was dropped because trailing execution is disabled\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-30\"></a>\n\n## Error 30: `DebounceCallDroppedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nDebounce call was dropped because trailing execution is disabled\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-31\"></a>\n\n## Error 31: `MissingMutationFunctionError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nmutationFn is required when creating a transaction\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-32\"></a>\n\n## Error 32: `OnMutateMustBeSynchronousError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nonMutate must be synchronous and cannot return a promise. Remove async/await or returned promises from onMutate.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-33\"></a>\n\n## Error 33: `TransactionNotPendingMutateError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nYou can no longer call .mutate() as the transaction is no longer pending\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-34\"></a>\n\n## Error 34: `TransactionAlreadyCompletedRollbackError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nYou can no longer call .rollback() as the transaction is already completed\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-35\"></a>\n\n## Error 35: `TransactionNotPendingCommitError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nYou can no longer call .commit() as the transaction is no longer pending\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-36\"></a>\n\n## Error 36: `NoPendingSyncTransactionWriteError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nNo pending sync transaction to write to\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-37\"></a>\n\n## Error 37: `SyncTransactionAlreadyCommittedWriteError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nThe pending sync transaction is already committed, you can't still write to it.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-38\"></a>\n\n## Error 38: `SyncRowReusedWithoutPreviousValueError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nA sync update for key \"key-1\" wrote a row object that changed in place since it was last written. The change overwrote the row's previous value. Write a new object, or pass the row's previous value as `previousValue`.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-39\"></a>\n\n## Error 39: `NoPendingSyncTransactionCommitError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nNo pending sync transaction to commit\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-40\"></a>\n\n## Error 40: `SyncTransactionAlreadyCommittedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nThe pending sync transaction is already committed, you can't commit it again.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-41\"></a>\n\n## Error 41: `SyncQueueInvariantError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nSync queue invariant failed: invariant detail\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-42\"></a>\n\n## Error 42: `OnlyOneSourceAllowedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nOnly one source is allowed in the join clause\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-43\"></a>\n\n## Error 43: `SubQueryMustHaveFromClauseError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nA sub query passed to a join clause must have a from clause itself\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-44\"></a>\n\n## Error 44: `InvalidSourceError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid source for live query: The value provided for alias \"todos\" is not a Collection or subquery. Live queries only accept Collection instances or subqueries. Please ensure you're passing a valid Collection or QueryBuilder, not a plain array or other data type.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-45\"></a>\n\n## Error 45: `InvalidSourceTypeError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid source for from clause: Expected an object with a single key-value pair like { alias: collection }. For example: .from({ todos: todosCollection }). Got: string\n```\n\n```text\nInvalid source for join clause: Expected an object with a single key-value pair like { alias: collection }. For example: .join({ todos: todosCollection }, ({ todo, todos }) => eq(todo.id, todos.id)). Got: number\n```\n\n```text\nInvalid source for unionAll clause: Expected an object with one or more key-value pairs like { alias: collection }. For example: .unionAll({ todos: todosCollection, events: eventsCollection }). Got: undefined\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-46\"></a>\n\n## Error 46: `JoinConditionMustBeEqualityError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nJoin condition must be an equality expression or a nonempty conjunction of equality expressions\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-47\"></a>\n\n## Error 47: `QueryMustHaveFromClauseError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nQuery must have a from clause\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-48\"></a>\n\n## Error 48: `InvalidWhereExpressionError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid where() expression: Expected a query expression, but received a boolean. This usually happens when using JavaScript's comparison operators (===, !==, <, >, etc.) directly. Instead, use the query builder functions:\n\n  ❌ .where(({ user }) => user.id === 'abc')\n  ✅ .where(({ user }) => eq(user.id, 'abc'))\n\nAvailable comparison functions: eq, gt, gte, lt, lte, and, or, not, like, ilike, isNull, isUndefined\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-49\"></a>\n\n## Error 49: `UnsafeAliasPathError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUnsafe alias path segment \"__proto__\" is not allowed in .select(). Aliases must not contain \"__proto__\", \"prototype\", or \"constructor\".\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-50\"></a>\n\n## Error 50: `DistinctRequiresSelectError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nDISTINCT requires a SELECT clause.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-51\"></a>\n\n## Error 51: `FnSelectWithGroupByError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nfn.select() cannot be used with groupBy(). groupBy requires the compiler to statically analyze aggregate functions (count, sum, max, etc.) in the SELECT clause, which is not possible with fn.select() since it is an opaque function. Use .select() instead of .fn.select() when combining with groupBy().\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-52\"></a>\n\n## Error 52: `UnsupportedFnSelectResultError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nfn.select() cannot return query builder. Child query builders, query expressions, and helpers such as eq(), toArray(), materialize(), concat(toArray()), and caseWhen() are query-construction values. Use them as direct fields in .select() instead.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-53\"></a>\n\n## Error 53: `UnsupportedRootScalarSelectError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nTop-level scalar select() is not supported by createLiveQueryCollection() or queryOnce(). Return an object from .select(), or use the scalar query inside toArray(...) or concat(toArray(...)).\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-54\"></a>\n\n## Error 54: `HavingRequiresGroupByError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nHAVING clause requires GROUP BY clause\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-55\"></a>\n\n## Error 55: `LimitOffsetRequireOrderByError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nLIMIT and OFFSET require an ORDER BY clause to ensure deterministic results\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-56\"></a>\n\n## Error 56: `CollectionInputNotFoundError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInput for alias \"alias\" (collection \"collection-1\") not found in inputs map. Available keys: key1, key2\n```\n\n```text\nInput for collection \"alias\" not found in inputs map\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-57\"></a>\n\n## Error 57: `DuplicateAliasInSubqueryError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nSubquery uses alias \"alias\" which is already used in the parent query. Each alias must be unique across parent and subquery contexts. Parent query aliases: parent1, parent2. Please rename \"alias\" in either the parent query or subquery to avoid conflicts.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-58\"></a>\n\n## Error 58: `UnsupportedFromTypeError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUnsupported FROM type: string\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-59\"></a>\n\n## Error 59: `UnknownExpressionTypeError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUnknown expression type: custom\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-60\"></a>\n\n## Error 60: `EmptyReferencePathError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nReference path cannot be empty\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-61\"></a>\n\n## Error 61: `UnknownFunctionError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUnknown function: customFn\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-62\"></a>\n\n## Error 62: `JoinCollectionNotFoundError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection \"collection-1\" not found during compilation of join\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-63\"></a>\n\n## Error 63: `UnsupportedJoinTypeError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUnsupported join type: OUTER\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-64\"></a>\n\n## Error 64: `InvalidJoinConditionSameSourceError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid join condition: both expressions refer to the same source \"todos\"\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-65\"></a>\n\n## Error 65: `InvalidJoinConditionSourceMismatchError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid join condition: expressions must reference source aliases\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-66\"></a>\n\n## Error 66: `InvalidJoinConditionLeftSourceError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid join condition: left expression refers to an unavailable source \"todos\"\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-67\"></a>\n\n## Error 67: `InvalidJoinConditionRightSourceError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid join condition: right expression does not refer to the joined source \"comments\"\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-68\"></a>\n\n## Error 68: `InvalidJoinCondition`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInvalid join condition\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-69\"></a>\n\n## Error 69: `UnsupportedJoinSourceTypeError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUnsupported join source type: custom\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-70\"></a>\n\n## Error 70: `NonAggregateExpressionNotInGroupByError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nNon-aggregate expression 'field' in SELECT must also appear in GROUP BY clause\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-71\"></a>\n\n## Error 71: `UnsupportedAggregateFunctionError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUnsupported aggregate function: customAgg\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-72\"></a>\n\n## Error 72: `AggregateFunctionNotInSelectError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nAggregate function in HAVING clause must also be in SELECT clause: count\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-73\"></a>\n\n## Error 73: `UnknownHavingExpressionTypeError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nUnknown expression type in HAVING clause: custom\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-74\"></a>\n\n## Error 74: `SerializationError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCannot write item because it cannot be JSON serialized: circular reference\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-75\"></a>\n\n## Error 75: `StorageKeyRequiredError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\n[LocalStorageCollection] storageKey must be provided.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-76\"></a>\n\n## Error 76: `InvalidStorageDataFormatError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\n[LocalStorageCollection] Invalid data format in storage key \"storageKey\" for key \"key\".\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-77\"></a>\n\n## Error 77: `InvalidStorageObjectFormatError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\n[LocalStorageCollection] Invalid data format in storage key \"storageKey\". Expected object format.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-78\"></a>\n\n## Error 78: `SyncCleanupError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection \"collection-1\" sync cleanup function threw an error: Cleanup failed\n```\n\n```text\nCollection \"collection-1\" sync cleanup function threw an error: Cleanup threw\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-79\"></a>\n\n## Error 79: `SyncTransactionAbortedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nSync transaction was aborted before application\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-80\"></a>\n\n## Error 80: `CollectionPreloadAbortedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCollection preload was abandoned during cleanup\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-81\"></a>\n\n## Error 81: `LoadSubsetOperationAbortedError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nLoad subset operation was aborted before its result became visible\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-82\"></a>\n\n## Error 82: `CannotCombineEmptyExpressionListError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nCannot combine empty expression list\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-83\"></a>\n\n## Error 83: `MissingAliasInputsError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nInternal error: compiler returned aliases without inputs: alias1, alias2. This indicates a bug in query compilation. Please report this issue.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-84\"></a>\n\n## Error 84: `SetWindowRequiresOrderByError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nsetWindow() can only be called on collections with an ORDER BY clause. Add .orderBy() to your query to enable window movement.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-85\"></a>\n\n## Error 85: `SetWindowReentrancyError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nsetWindow() cannot run reentrantly. Wait for the current window operation to return before starting another one.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-86\"></a>\n\n## Error 86: `PacedTransactionManualCommitError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nPaced mutations are committed by their strategy. Await the transaction receipt or roll it back instead.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-87\"></a>\n\n## Error 87: `UnhashableQueryIRError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nQuery IR is not stably hashable at query.fnSelect: function select\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-175\"></a>\n\n## Error 175: `DatabaseRequiredError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nIndexedDB collection requires a \"db\" configuration option. Create a database instance using createIndexedDB() and pass it to the collection.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-176\"></a>\n\n## Error 176: `ObjectStoreNotFoundError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nObject store \"todos\" not found in database \"app\". Available stores: [users, posts]. Add \"todos\" to the stores array when calling createIndexedDB().\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-177\"></a>\n\n## Error 177: `NameRequiredError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nIndexedDB collection requires a \"name\" configuration option. This is the name of the object store within the database.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-178\"></a>\n\n## Error 178: `GetKeyRequiredError`\n\nDevelopment builds show the full message. For example:\n\n```text\nIndexedDB collection requires a \"getKey\" configuration option. This function extracts the unique key from each item.\n```\n\n## Other errors and log messages\n\nThese are plain `Error`, `TypeError`, `RangeError`, or\n`AggregateError` values, and `console` messages about runtime failures.\nEach heading names the source file under `packages/db/src` that writes it.\n\n<a id=\"error-88\"></a>\n\n## Error 88: `client.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\ncollectionOptions requires a non-empty explicit id so the descriptor is stable across DbClient instances and SSR boundaries.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-89\"></a>\n\n## Error 89: `client.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\ncollectionOptions(\"${id}\") requires a factory as its second argument.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-90\"></a>\n\n## Error 90: `client.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nCollection descriptor \"${id}\" was created from a concrete config that cannot be safely reused across DbClient instances. Use collectionOptions(\"${id}\", (client) => adapterCollectionOptions(...)) or an adapter options creator that supports DbClient materialization.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-91\"></a>\n\n## Error 91: `client.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nCollection descriptor \"${id}\" materialized a config with id \"${materialized.id}\". Descriptor and collection ids must match.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-92\"></a>\n\n## Error 92: `client.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nDbClient is missing the required \"${key}\" dependency. Pass it explicitly when constructing the client: new DbClient({ ${key} }).\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-93\"></a>\n\n## Error 93: `client.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nDehydrated live query \"${dehydratedQuery.queryHash}\" has neither a snapshot nor a promise.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-94\"></a>\n\n## Error 94: `collection/change-events.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nlimit cannot be used without orderBy\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-95\"></a>\n\n## Error 95: `collection/changes.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nCannot specify both 'where' and 'whereExpression' options. Use one or the other.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-96\"></a>\n\n## Error 96: `collection/subscription.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nlimit is required\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-97\"></a>\n\n## Error 97: `collection/subscription.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nOrdered snapshot was requested but no index was found. You have to call setOrderByIndex before requesting an ordered snapshot.\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-98\"></a>\n\n## Error 98: `event-emitter.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nTimeout waiting for event ${String(event)}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-99\"></a>\n\n## Error 99: `indexes/base-index.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nFailed to evaluate index expression for key ${key}: ${error}\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-100\"></a>\n\n## Error 100: `indexes/basic-index.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nOperation ${operation} not supported by BasicIndex\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-101\"></a>\n\n## Error 101: `indexes/btree-index.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by values:\n\n```text\nOperation ${operation} not supported by BTreeIndex\n```\n\n<a id=\"error-102\"></a>\n\n## Error 102: `live-query-options.ts`\n\nDevelopment builds show this message, with `${...}` replaced by valu